{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/120938-non-evil-dark-virtues","id":120938,"title":"Non-Evil Dark Virtues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-28T08:10:59-07:00","id":120938,"title":"Non-Evil Dark Virtues","content":"Does anyone have ideas for alternate Dark Virtues which are more morally ambiguous than the original four? The only suggestion I've seen (on the old forum) was &quot;Fecundity&quot;, which might be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T10:10:13-07:00","id":121004,"title":"","content":"If I were to change them I would probably go with something more primal to fit the nature of the Titans. The problem with this is that it makes anything with Dark virtues seem more alien, or at least animalistic. Fecundity, certainly fits that description. The desire to consume fits too, so I might keep Rapacity as it is or modify it slightly. I'd need to think more on what else I would do, but I could see the &quot;need to survive&quot; and the &quot;need to grow or evolve&quot; fitting a more primal nature. So basically the basic behaviors that describe life. Eat, Grow, Survive, Reproduce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:40:15-07:00","id":121122,"title":"","content":"Ambition, Rapacity, and Zealotry are already very morally ambiguous.<br /> Malice not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2447,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","user":"TwitchTheRat","date":". 04-28-2014, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T12:47:47-07:00","id":121133,"title":"","content":"<b>Malice</b> is the only Dark Virtue that stands out as being completely terrible because you need to go around torturing people.<br /> The rest of the Dark Virtues are much more neutral, and can even be a positive thing in certain circumstances.<br /> Honestly, there has been lot of discussion about how <b>Ambition</b> should not even be considered a &quot;Dark&quot; Virtue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T14:59:25-07:00","id":121244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to change them I would probably go with something more primal to fit the nature of the Titans. The problem with this is that it makes anything with Dark virtues seem more alien, or at least animalistic. Fecundity, certainly fits that description. The desire to consume fits too, so I might keep Rapacity as it is or modify it slightly. I'd need to think more on what else I would do, but I could see the &quot;need to survive&quot; and the &quot;need to grow or evolve&quot; fitting a more primal nature. So basically the basic behaviors that describe life. Eat, Grow, Survive, Reproduce.</div> </div> </div> </div> *nods* Perverting those endeavors that make up survival we could come up with some additions..maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T16:24:58-07:00","id":121285,"title":"","content":"Any of those ideas I proposed taken to either extreme could produce some very horrific personality traits for characters. They can also be expanded in non-standard ways, the need to eat could be expanded to be a need to possess, and turned into greed. The need to grow could produce an inventor as the person desires to grow beyond their own limitations. Survival taken to extremes could result in cowardly behavior, a desire to destroy any potential threats, or even lead to the character uploading their mind to the internet to exist as an immortal distributed intelligence. The need to reproduce can get pretty squicky in ways that I'd rather not discuss, but it could lead to things like cloning or robot armies, or something nice like the desire to defend a love or at least defend a mate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T20:29:46-07:00","id":121425,"title":"","content":"I just scrapped the concept of Dark Virtues. Ambition is a regular, every day Virtue for me. Rapacity and Malice exist as well, but while they're rather nasty things to have, they appear ALL OVER mythology and have no restriction to Titan-like figures. There's no way you can tell me that Tezcatlipoca hasn't got Malice, for example. Zealotry, however, I never understood. It's just... Evil Piety, really. So I scrapped it entirely, it doesn't exist at all in any form.<br /> <br /> So, I just give everyone the Virtues that fit them best, including Ambition (Hi, Odin!), Rapacity (How<i> you</i> doin', Zeus?) and Malice. My players still have a kinda knee-jerk reaction whenever they use a power to scan someone's Virtues and come up with one or mark &quot;Dark&quot; Virtues, but I keep reminding them that there are only Virtues.<br /> <br /> If you want less &quot;evil&quot; Dark Virtues.. I don't understand what you're asking, really. Those are just more Virtues. If they're not evil, why would they be Dark? The only thing that makes Dark Virtues Dark is that they're outright evil (which I tone down), compared to the regular Virtues which are only evil <i>sometimes</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T20:53:54-07:00","id":121439,"title":"","content":"I like this concept. It never made much sense to me that titans would have these all-consuming evil and horrific 'dark virtues' when they essentially represent fundamental forces of nature and existence. Nature is not evil or good, it simply IS. 'Dark virtues' sound like another ham-handed attempt to shoehorn christianized human morality into a system that deals with totally immoral creatures (titans) and things beyond the ken of mortal understanding (gods). I call into question the need for titans to even <i>have</i> virtues seeing as how they exist beyond the concept of morality altogether. Gods can have virtues since they invented them, and that can be one of the many things that sets them apart from the more primal titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T21:58:36-07:00","id":121487,"title":"","content":"Virtues aren't really about morality. They're about behavioral imperatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T05:15:51-07:00","id":121637,"title":"","content":"Ambition is definitely a gray spot to me. It's ok to have this drive for success. It's how its accomplished that shows the good/evil side of it. Also...just what is the exact nature of said ambition? If it's...for example, to &quot;enslave the Sudan&quot; or &quot;save the Sudanese from genocide&quot; then I'd say we can probably see the good/evil aspects fairly easily.<br /> <br /> Ah...the morality question. It seems to me that to be &quot;immoral&quot; or &quot;amoral&quot; is to separate oneself from the human race (and probably Life in general). The old system of titans can definitely be seen in this light I would think. However titans need a construct, some sort of order for them to exist. Some sort of cohesion for an ability to think and relate to other beings. Otherwise, how can they tempt scions to their &quot;side&quot; if they lack any coherent means to communicate, let alone to relate to that person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:04:55-07:00","id":121927,"title":"","content":"Here's an interesting blog post regarding Dark Virtues: <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2013/09/hearts-in-dark.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://johnsscionresources.blogspot....s-in-dark.html</a><br /> <br /> I do rather like Telgar's idea of doing away with &quot;Dark&quot; and just having everything be Virtues. It's an excellent way of thinking about it. And it removes the Christian buggery from the equation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T14:13:22-07:00","id":122657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/120938-non-evil-dark-virtues?p=121133#post121133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Malice</b> is the only Dark Virtue that stands out as being completely terrible because you need to go around torturing people.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet can be seen as a primal and animalistic thing - the natural world is full of messed up stuff animals will do with little to no qualms to other beings simply because the victims are smaller, so they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T14:44:44-07:00","id":122680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/120938-non-evil-dark-virtues?p=122657#post122657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet can be seen as a primal and animalistic thing - the natural world is full of messed up stuff animals will do with little to no qualms to other beings simply because the victims are smaller, so they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it can also be phrased as Paranoia: You're afraid of someone becoming a threat, so you take preemptive action to get them dead or get them to back off. And if someone's already proven a threat, well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T16:01:17-07:00","id":122726,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* Humans are supposed to know better than animals. Gods even more so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T17:36:36-07:00","id":123521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/120938-non-evil-dark-virtues?p=122726#post122726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* Humans are supposed to know better than animals. Gods even more so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans delude themselves in thinking their reasoning abilities make them better, but we are just as capable of wallowing in cruelty. It is the desire to resist this kind of urges, the comprehension of them as self-centered, harmful &amp; base and the willing surrendering of one's senses to such behaviour as a bad thing that makes malice a <b>dark</b> virtue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T18:12:06-07:00","id":123535,"title":"","content":"I think you missed the point. Humans have that capacity for cruelty, just as they have the capacity for compassion. A conscious choice. I concede that there are a few animals that have a degree of capacity for that as well. But it's typically not the case. Survival is the chief instinct for most critters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:01:00-07:00","id":124025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/120938-non-evil-dark-virtues?p=123535#post123535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you missed the point. Humans have that capacity for cruelty, just as they have the capacity for compassion. A conscious choice. I concede that there are a few animals that have a degree of capacity for that as well. But it's typically not the case. Survival is the chief instinct for most critters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same could be said about Compassion or Order - Virtues as a whole are rationalization of certain instincts or impulses. Dark Virtues represent those self-centered impulses transformed into rational &amp; passional, though not exactly moral, behaviour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T05:45:57-07:00","id":126643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/120938-non-evil-dark-virtues?p=122726#post122726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* Humans are supposed to know better than animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gods even more so. </div> </div> </div>Hah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T15:30:59-07:00","id":127024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/120938-non-evil-dark-virtues?p=121487#post121487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Virtues aren't really about morality. They're about behavioral imperatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the most succinct argument I\u2019ve ever seen for ditching the concept of \u201cDark Virtues\u201d outright. I definitely agree on the notion of doing away with Dark Virtues and the related tendency to pigeonhole anyone who has them as cardboard-cutout villains. <br /> <br /> Prometheus was a Titan. In 1e, that required some hoop-jumping to explain why it makes sense for him to be malicious, rapacious, zealous, and ambitious. I hope that 2e will allow for more flexibility with Titans; and to the extent that they\u2019re still the go-to villains of the game, I\u2019d rather they display dark portrayals of Virtues instead of distinct Dark Virtues: \u201cPiety at its worst\u201d rather than \u201cZealotry\u201d. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T05:42:03-07:00","id":127406,"title":"","content":"I strongly agree with those who argue Ambition (especially) and Rapacity are vanilla Virtues that may be appropriate for several Gods and Scion character concepts. I could easily see Ambition as a Virtue of the Yankee Pantheon. Zealotry is simply a Titan-oriented version of Piety. Malice, while being of a darker shade than the rest, may still fit certain Gods that have no love for the Titans. Really, there is no good reason why the drive to self-empowerment and get ahead should be seen as inherently evil. Usual WW effort to pigeonhole Christianized morality where it does not belong and shove it down the player's throats. This reminds me to ask, what are the durations for Overweening Arrogance, Reckless Hunger, and All-Consuming Hatred ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-07-2014, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T08:41:20-07:00","id":127496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/120938-non-evil-dark-virtues?p=124025#post124025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same could be said about Compassion or Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compassion is not a Virtue. And it probably should never be, mostly because Virtues are not really virtues in the literal sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T12:21:06-07:00","id":128444,"title":"","content":"In honesty Vengeance is not a Virtue either. And Dark Virtue just sounds odd. Why don't they just call them a Vice. Hell, some gods definitely have Vices that they are well known for as has been mentioned earlier. I'm much more for the idea that the Titans are more layered beings like the gods are instead of this one dimensional entity of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T13:20:24-07:00","id":128471,"title":"","content":"From a titan perspective, one god's virtue is another god's vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T11:16:03-07:00","id":130012,"title":"","content":"(Due to computer problems, I can access only the first page of a thread, so my apologies if someone has said this already.) <br /> <br /> Mm, I think it's less a &quot;Christianizing&quot; influence than a &quot;Gamerizing&quot; influence. Giving the Titans their own set of Virtues, and explicitly defining them as &quot;Dark&quot; and evil, creates unambiguous Bad Guys for the PCs to oppose. Which makes it easy for gamers. <br /> <br /> I'm not a big fan of the result, for reasons that others have already stated. Though I'm not a fan of the Virtue system overall, either. I hope the whole subject receives a close examination and reworking in Scion 2.0. <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}